Canva today released <a href="https://www.affinity.studio/ipad-app">Affinity for iPad</a>, bringing its free all-in-one design app to Apple's tablet, along with a new Sketch Studio built for touch and Apple Pencil.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/affinity-by-canva-ipad2.jpg" alt="affinity" width="2340" height="1316" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075010" /><br/>
The release follows last year's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/31/canva-relaunches-affinity-free-app/">desktop app relaunch</a>, which combined the previously separate Affinity Designer, Photo, and Publisher apps into a single app for Mac and Windows. Canva had promised an iPad version in 2026, and says the desktop app has since attracted more than seven million sign-ups.<br/>
<br/>
The iPad app brings sketching, vector graphics, photo editing, and page layout together in one interface. Users can switch between Sketch, Vector, Pixel, and Layout studios while working in the same .af file, which can also be opened on desktop.<br/>
<br/>
Sketch Studio adds freehand drawing with a customizable brush library, while Sketch to Shapes turns hand-drawn forms into editable vector shapes. Photo tools include RAW editing, non-destructive adjustments, and a Mask Tool designed to help trace difficult edges such as hair and fur with Apple Pencil. Elsewhere, layout tools support multi-page documents, master pages, and print-ready output.<br/>
<br/>
Canva says the interface has been designed specifically for iPad rather than scaled down from the desktop app. As for Apple Pencil Pro support, it includes barrel roll, squeeze, and hover, alongside pressure and tilt controls.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/affinity-by-canva-ipad1-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075011" /><br/>
The core sketching, vector, photo, and layout tools are free for individuals, but a free Canva account is required to use the app. The only paid-for features are the AI tools, which are locked behind a Canva premium plan – continuing the approach introduced with 2025's desktop relaunch.<br/>
<br/>
The paid features are available through Canva AI Studio and include Generative Expand, image upscaling, noise reduction, and Decompose Layer, which splits a flat image into editable layers.<br/>
<br/>
Despite the shared file format, some desktop features are missing from the iPad version at launch. <a href="https://www.affinity.studio/ipad-app">Affinity's website</a> lists Books, Batch, Data Merge, Quick Adjustments, Info and Scope panels, macro recording, and Astrophotography Studio among the omissions, with more features planned over time.<br/>
<br/>
